  "docs": {
    "sheet/close.md": "<!-- Generated from the blueprint. Do not edit. -->\n# sheet.close\n\nTake a sheet down. Nobody can join it after this.\n\n**Who may call:** anyone.\n\n**Budget:** p95 150ms.\n\n## Payload\n\n| field | value |\n|---|---|\n| sheet | sheet.id |\n\n## Answer\n\n(none)\n\n## Move\n\n`close`: from open or full to closed, emitting SheetClosed.\n\n## Steps\n\n- `sheet.close.record` (database)\n\n## Refusals\n\n| refusal | exit | code | when |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| SheetNotOpen | 70 | SH-900 | the sheet is in a state close can't start from; carries `state` |\n| SheetNotFound | 4 | SH-901 | nothing has the id in sheet; the handler never runs; carries `id` |\n\n## Worked examples\n\n### a closed sheet takes no one\n\nStarts from the world `opened`.\n\n- **the visitor closes the sheet.** `visitor` (anyone) calls and sends sheet the world's sheet, and is answered.\n- **closing it again is refused.** `visitor` (anyone) calls and sends sheet the world's sheet, and is refused with SheetNotOpen, SH-900, carrying state `closed`.\n\n## How to call\n\n```sh\nsignup sheet close --sheet <sheet>\n```\n\nHTTP: `POST /sheet/close` with the payload as JSON. SDK: `Sdk.sheet.close(payload)`.\n",
    "sheet/get.md": "<!-- Generated from the blueprint. Do not edit. -->\n# sheet.get\n\nRead one sheet by its id: title, places, taken, state.\n\n**Who may call:** anyone.\n\n**A read:** answered from the records, with no handler.\n\n**Budget:** p95 50ms.\n\n## Payload\n\n| field | value |\n|---|---|\n| id | sheet.id |\n\n## Answer\n\n| field | value |\n|---|---|\n| title | sheet.title |\n| places | sheet.places |\n| taken | sheet.taken |\n| state | text |\n\n## Refusals\n\n(none)\n\n## Worked examples\n\n### a closed sheet takes no one\n\nStarts from the world `opened`.\n\n- **reading it back shows a closed sheet with nobody on it.** `visitor` (anyone) calls and sends id the world's sheet, and gets back [`0`, `closed`].\n\n### fill a sheet\n\nStarts from the world `opened`.\n\n- **reading it back shows both places taken.** `visitor` (anyone) calls and sends id the world's sheet, and gets back [`2`, `2`, `full`].\n\n### join twice with one request\n\nStarts from the world `opened`.\n\n- **only one place was taken.** `visitor` (anyone) calls and sends id the world's sheet, and gets back [`1`, `open`].\n\n### put up a sheet\n\nStarts from an empty world.\n\n- **reading it back shows an open sheet with nobody on it.** `visitor` (anyone) calls and sends id the last call's sheet, and gets back [`Book club`, `3`, `0`, `open`].\n\n## How to call\n\n```sh\nsignup sheet get --id <id>\n```\n\nHTTP: `POST /sheet/get` with the payload as JSON. SDK: `Sdk.sheet.get(payload)`.\n",
    "sheet/index.md": "<!-- Generated from the blueprint. Do not edit. -->\n# sheet\n\nA sign-up sheet with a fixed number of places.\n\nLives in the database.\n\n## Fields\n\n| field | value |\n|---|---|\n| id | id |\n| title | Title |\n| places | Count |\n| taken | Count |\n\n## Machine\n\nStates: open, full, closed. A move from the wrong state is refused SheetNotOpen (exit 70).\n\n| move | from | to | emits |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| open | (creates) | open | SheetOpened |\n| join | open | open, full | PlaceTaken |\n| close | open, full | closed | SheetClosed |\n\n## Events\n\n- `PlaceTaken`: carries sheet (sheet.id), left (Count); emitted by the move join\n- `SheetClosed`: carries sheet (sheet.id); emitted by the move close\n- `SheetOpened`: carries sheet (sheet.id), places (Count); emitted by the move open\n\n## Operations\n\n- [sheet.close](close.md): Take a sheet down. Nobody can join it after this.\n- [sheet.get](get.md): Read one sheet by its id: title, places, taken, state.\n- [sheet.join](join.md): Take places on a sheet, for yourself and anyone with you.\n- [sheet.open](open.md): Put up a sheet with a number of places.\n",
    "sheet/join.md": "<!-- Generated from the blueprint. Do not edit. -->\n# sheet.join\n\nTake places on a sheet, for yourself and anyone with you.\n\n**Who may call:** anyone.\n\n**Idempotent by request:** send `idempotency-key`; the same key twice is one call.\n\n**Budget:** p95 150ms.\n\n## Payload\n\n| field | value |\n|---|---|\n| sheet | sheet.id |\n| people | Count |\n\n## Answer\n\n| field | value |\n|---|---|\n| left | Count |\n\n## Move\n\n`join`: from open to open or full, emitting PlaceTaken.\n\n## Steps\n\n- `sheet.join.load` (database)\n- `sheet.join.record` (database)\n\n## Refusals\n\n| refusal | exit | code | when |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| SheetFull | 71 | SH-001 | declared in errors.ts, carrying left |\n| SheetNotOpen | 70 | SH-900 | the sheet is in a state join can't start from; carries `state` |\n| SheetNotFound | 4 | SH-901 | nothing has the id in sheet; the handler never runs; carries `id` |\n| IdempotencyConflict | 120 | AR-002 | the request key was first used with another payload; the handler never runs |\n\n## Worked examples\n\n### a closed sheet takes no one\n\nStarts from the world `opened`.\n\n- **joining it is refused.** `visitor` (anyone) calls and sends sheet the world's sheet, people `1`, with the request key `late-1`, and is refused with SheetNotOpen, SH-900, carrying state `closed`.\n\n### fill a sheet\n\nStarts from the world `opened`.\n\n- **the first join leaves one place and the sheet stays open.** `visitor` (anyone) calls and sends sheet the world's sheet, people `1`, with the request key `join-1`, and gets back `1`.\n- **two people are refused: only one place is left.** `visitor` (anyone) calls and sends sheet the world's sheet, people `2`, with the request key `join-2-people`, and is refused with SheetFull, SH-001, carrying left `1`.\n- **the second join takes the last place and the sheet is full.** `visitor` (anyone) calls and sends sheet the world's sheet, people `1`, with the request key `join-3`, and gets back `0`.\n- **a third join is refused: a full sheet is not open.** `visitor` (anyone) calls and sends sheet the world's sheet, people `1`, with the request key `join-4`, and is refused with SheetNotOpen, SH-900, carrying state `full`.\n\n### join twice with one request\n\nStarts from the world `opened`.\n\n- **the visitor joins.** `visitor` (anyone) calls and sends sheet the world's sheet, people `1`, with the request key `me-1`, and gets back `1`.\n- **the same request again gives the same answer and takes nothing.** `visitor` (anyone) calls and sends sheet the world's sheet, people `1`, with the request key `me-1`, and gets back `1`.\n\n## How to call\n\n```sh\nsignup sheet join --sheet <sheet> --people <people>\n```\n\nHTTP: `POST /sheet/join` with the payload as JSON. SDK: `Sdk.sheet.join(payload)`.\n",
    "sheet/open.md": "<!-- Generated from the blueprint. Do not edit. -->\n# sheet.open\n\nPut up a sheet with a number of places.\n\n**Who may call:** anyone.\n\n**Idempotent by request:** send `idempotency-key`; the same key twice is one call.\n\n**Budget:** p95 150ms.\n\n## Payload\n\n| field | value |\n|---|---|\n| title | sheet.title |\n| places | sheet.places |\n\n## Answer\n\n| field | value |\n|---|---|\n| sheet | sheet.id |\n\n## Move\n\n`open`: from nothing (it creates) to open, emitting SheetOpened.\n\n## Steps\n\n- `sheet.open.insert` (database)\n\n## Refusals\n\n| refusal | exit | code | when |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| IdempotencyConflict | 120 | AR-002 | the request key was first used with another payload; the handler never runs |\n\n## Worked examples\n\n### put up a sheet\n\nStarts from an empty world.\n\n- **a visitor puts up a sheet with 3 places.** `visitor` (anyone) calls and sends title `Book club`, places `3`, and gets back an answer matching `^sht_`.\n\n## How to call\n\n```sh\nsignup sheet open --title <title> --places <places>\n```\n\nHTTP: `POST /sheet/open` with the payload as JSON. SDK: `Sdk.sheet.open(payload)`.\n"
  },
